---
---

<div class="space-y-6">
  <!-- Knowledge Header -->
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-3">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        🏛️ The Four Pillars of Sustainable Personal Finance
      </h2>
      <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[10px] font-bold bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-800 border border-emerald-200 uppercase tracking-wider">
        Educational Blueprint
      </span>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
      Lasting financial security is not built on speculative bets or short-term windfalls. It rests on a four-pillar framework designed to master day-to-day cash flow, eliminate high-cost liabilities, compound productive investments, and preserve purchasing power across every stage of life.
    </p>

    <!-- Four Pillars Road Map Banner -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-2.5 pt-2">
      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-emerald-800">
          <span>💧</span> Pillar 1
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-900">Mindful Cash Flow</div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500">Living below your means & capturing regular margin.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-sky-800">
          <span>🛡️</span> Pillar 2
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-900">Debt & Risk Shield</div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500">Emergency buffer, insurance, and debt payoff.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-indigo-800">
          <span>📈</span> Pillar 3
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-900">Wealth Accumulation</div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500">Systematic investing & long-term compounding.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-teal-800">
          <span>🏰</span> Pillar 4
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-900">Preservation & Freedom</div>
        <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500">Inflation defense, tax efficiency, and autonomy.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- The Four Pillars Detailed Cards Grid -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
    <!-- PILLAR 1: Mindful Cash Flow & Budgeting -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-4 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl border border-emerald-100">
            💧
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700">Pillar 1 • The Foundation</span>
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
              Cash Flow & Mindful Budgeting
            </h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[10px] font-semibold bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">Cash Flow Margin</span>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Sustainable wealth is impossible without a consistent positive gap between what you earn and what you consume. Pillar 1 establishes disciplined control over your daily inflows and outflows.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-2.5 text-xs">
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">1. Pay Yourself First (Automated Habit)</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Rather than attempting to save whatever happens to remain at the month's conclusion, set an automated transfer to savings or investments immediately upon salary credit.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">2. The 50 / 30 / 20 Allocation Framework</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Allocate ~50% to essential obligations (housing, groceries, utilities), ~30% to discretionary enjoyment (dining, leisure), and at least 20% directly toward savings and debt pre-payment.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">3. Taming Silent Spending Leaks & Lifestyle Creep</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Audit recurring digital subscriptions, quick-commerce impulses, and convenient delivery fees quarterly. Direct at least half of each income raise into investments rather than expanding recurring overhead.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PILLAR 2: Debt Optimization & Risk Protection -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-4 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-sky-50 text-sky-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl border border-sky-100">
            🛡️
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-700">Pillar 2 • The Shield</span>
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
              Debt Optimization & Risk Protection
            </h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[10px] font-semibold bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">Capital Defense</span>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Financial progress can be quickly undone by high-interest liabilities or unexpected medical events. Pillar 2 constructs an unshakeable protective fortress around your family balance sheet.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-2.5 text-xs">
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">1. Eliminating High-Interest Liabilities</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Prioritize clearing revolving credit card debt (often 36%–44% p.a.) and unsecured personal loans using the Avalanche (interest-minimizing) or Snowball (milestone-building) model.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">2. The 3-to-6 Month Emergency Buffer</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Park 3 to 6 months of mandatory living expenses in safe, liquid instruments (such as auto-sweep term deposits or liquid mutual funds) to insulate your investments from forced liquidation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">3. Comprehensive Pure Insurance Coverage</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Protect financial dependents with pure term life insurance (advised at 10x–15x annual income) alongside robust family health insurance to safeguard personal assets from medical inflation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PILLAR 3: Disciplined Wealth Accumulation -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-4 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl border border-indigo-100">
            📈
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-700">Pillar 3 • The Engine</span>
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
              Disciplined Wealth Accumulation
            </h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[10px] font-semibold bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">Compounding Engine</span>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Accumulating lasting wealth relies on consistency, patient compounding, and diversified asset allocation rather than market speculation or timing.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-2.5 text-xs">
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">1. The Power of Systematic Investing (SIP / DCA)</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Investing fixed sums regularly into diversified index funds or mutual funds averages acquisition costs over market volatility cycles and instills unwavering financial discipline.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">2. The Rule of 72 & Exponential Growth</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Divide 72 by your expected annual yield to approximate doubling timelines. Compounding accelerates non-linearly over decades: time in the market is vastly more critical than timing entry points.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">3. Goal-Oriented Asset Allocation</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Match asset classes to your time horizon: short-term goals (<3 years) belong in stable debt instruments, whereas long-term horizons (>7 years) benefit from broad equity growth.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PILLAR 4: Long-Term Preservation & Autonomy -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-4 hover:border-slate-300 transition-colors">
      <div class="flex items-start justify-between">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-teal-50 text-teal-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl border border-teal-100">
            🏰
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-teal-700">Pillar 4 • The Pinnacle</span>
            <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
              Preservation, Autonomy & Freedom
            </h3>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-[10px] font-semibold bg-slate-100 text-slate-700">Time Autonomy</span>
      </div>

      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        The ultimate purpose of wealth is not consumption, but self-determination—the freedom to manage your time, protect purchasing power against inflation, and achieve complete autonomy.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-2.5 text-xs">
        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">1. Defeating Purchasing Power Erosion (Inflation)</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Cash left idle in low-yield savings accounts loses purchasing power over time. Structuring your portfolio to generate real (inflation-adjusted) yields preserves your hard-earned wealth.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">2. Tax-Aware Efficiency & Low Drag</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Utilize recognized tax-efficient instruments (such as PPF, EPF, NPS, or long-term capital gains exemptions) to minimize avoidable friction on compounding assets.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
          <strong class="text-slate-900 block font-semibold">3. Achieving True Financial Independence</strong>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            When passive yields from productive assets comfortably fund baseline living expenses, work becomes an intentional choice rather than an economic obligation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Essential Financial Glossary & Benchmarks -->
  <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-xs space-y-4">
    <div class="border-b border-slate-100 pb-3">
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 font-['Outfit',sans-serif]">
        Core Benchmarks & Glossary for Sustainable Personal Finance
      </h3>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-0.5">
        Practical rules of thumb and key terms to evaluate your personal financial foundation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-xs">
      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Cash Flow Margin</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">The surplus remaining after deducting monthly essential and discretionary living expenses from net take-home earnings. This margin fuels all wealth building.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Debt-to-Income / FOIR</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">Fixed Obligation to Income Ratio: the proportion of take-home income committed to mandatory loan EMIs and dues. Prudent guidelines advise keeping this below 40%.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Compounding & Rule of 72</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">Reinvesting earned returns so that returns generate their own returns. Divide 72 by the annual return rate to approximate how many years capital takes to double.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Emergency Shield</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">Liquid reserves covering 3 to 6 months of baseline living costs kept in safe, immediately accessible instruments such as sweep-in FDs or liquid funds.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Real vs. Nominal Return</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">Nominal return is the stated interest or capital gain; real return subtracts the inflation rate to reveal actual purchasing power expansion.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/80 space-y-1">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-900">Financial Independence (FI)</span>
        <p class="text-slate-600">The milestone at which accumulated wealth generates sufficient recurring sustainable cash flow to cover essential life expenses indefinitely without active employment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
